{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And Reuben returned to the pit.</b> Rashi explained that he was occupied with his sackcloth and his fasting on account of the disruption of his father's beds. And if you ask: in tractate Makkot it concludes, 'what caused Reuben to confess? Judah, etc.' — the implication is that Reuben did not confess until after Judah confessed regarding the matter of Tamar, which was after the sale of Joseph. And one may answer that he did not confess publicly until Judah confessed, but in private he repented and would wear sackcloth."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:33.506844026Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}